Coherent implementation, validation, delivery, and task recovery

Install:
  Install the missing bundled skill; preserve detected installed copies.
  Add or replace Codex developer_instructions to read and follow coherent-change for changes and reread it after context compaction or a handoff, including when the skill is already installed.

Upgrade:
  Back up and replace the installed skill with Wsley's bundled files; restore previous copies if replacement fails.
  Update Codex developer_instructions when the skill is installed; skip both operations when it is missing.

Status:
  Report skill locations based on SKILL.md presence.
  Report whether Codex developer_instructions matches the managed instruction.

Requirements:
  A regular user, AWK and standard file utilities.

Configuration:
  Destination: ~/.agents/skills/coherent-change
  The bundled skill guides ordinary development, fixes, refactoring and configuration changes, keeping task requirements, project rules, callers, resources and verification aligned.
  Default rules cover responsibility boundaries, complete migrations, comments and output languages, verification costs, artifact directories and documentation authorization; explicit user requirements and project rules take precedence.
  In-flight guidance updates task requirements or adds work to finish before resuming the original task; completed items retain their results, validation evidence and reporting status.
  Context compaction and handoffs restore unfinished work, continuing constraints and working state; unaffected completed items are not reopened or reported again on each recovery.
  Existing copies at ${CODEX_HOME:-$HOME/.codex}/skills/coherent-change are consolidated into links to the destination when skill files are replaced.
  Codex configuration: ${CODEX_HOME:-$HOME/.codex}/config.toml
  developer_instructions = "Read and follow the coherent-change skill before changing code, configuration, or scripts. After context compaction or a handoff, reread it and resume unfinished work."
  Replace the entire developer_instructions value; preserve other settings and back up the configuration before its first change.
